1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:01,120
Waiting for a rate cut

2
00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:02,780
isn't a property strategy.

3
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,840
A rate cut might ease the repayments.

4
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:05,620
It won't tell you

5
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,510
whether your next

6
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,560
property actually stacks up.

7
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,710
Before you borrow more,

8
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:12,810
look at the repayments,

9
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:14,160
the ongoing costs,

10
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:14,910
and what happens if

11
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,640
rates stay higher than you hoped.

12
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,140
Equity can give you options.

13
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,300
Using it means taking on more debt.

14
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,140
I'm Brian from Strategic Investing.

15
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:23,550
Before your next move,

16
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,480
let's discuss your options.

